<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠσχο-φόρια</span></b> , τά, one
		day of the Athen. festival <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκίρα,</span> on
		which two chosen young men, sons of citizens, in women's dress, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carrying vine-shoots loaded with
				grapes</i> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠσχός</span>), went
			in procession from the temple of Dionysus to that of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηνᾶ Σκιράς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> sg. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠσχο-φόριον</span></b> , τό, the sanctuary of Athena <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκιράς</span> in Phalerum,
				<i><span class="en">Hsch.,
				<u>AB</u>318</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
